# --- environments ----------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

# --- data: never in git ----------------------------------------------------
# Raw sonar is large and often licence-restricted. Acquisition is scripted in
# ai/scripts/ and documented in docs/DATA.md so a clone can rebuild it.
# Ignore contents, keep the directory itself so a fresh clone has the tree.
ai/data/raw/*
ai/data/interim/*
ai/data/processed/*
ai/data/hard_negatives/*
ai/data/metadata/raw/*
ai/data/metadata/normalized/*
ai/data/annotations/raw/*
ai/data/annotations/normalized/*

# ai/data/provenance/ is NOT ignored, on purpose. dataset_candidates.csv and
# data_inventory.csv are small text records of where data came from, what
# licence it carries and what is actually on disk. They are the audit trail the
# plan's provenance requirement asks for -- losing them costs more than the few
# kilobytes they take.
*.xtf
*.jsf
*.sdf

# ai/data/annotate/ holds hand-drawn ground truth: the ONLY labels in this
# project that were produced here rather than inherited, and the only ones no
# download can replace. The labels are committed. The image copies beside them
# are not -- they are re-fetchable from China-Offshore-SSS-AI and KLSG, and
# they are 29 MB.
#
# _guide/ IS committed: it is the worked examples that define the annotation
# convention, and taxonomy.py points a reader at it to explain what a
# ghost_net box means. A convention nobody can see is a convention nobody can
# reproduce. Recompressed to 1.4 MB for that reason.
ai/data/annotate/*/images/
# Transient overlays from check_annotations.py --render. Regenerated on demand.
ai/data/annotate/*/review_*.png

# --- model weights ---------------------------------------------------------
# Pretrained weights are re-downloadable (ai/scripts/fetch_weights.py).
# Training artefacts stay out -- every run produces a set and they are large.
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.engine
ai/models/pretrained/*
ai/models/trained/*

# ...except the deployed model. 18 MB, and without it the backend silently
# falls back to MockAIAdapter, so a fresh clone would show invented detections.
# Shipping it is what lets anyone do a real end-to-end run. See docs/SETUP.md.
!ai/models/trained/ghostnet.pt
!ai/models/trained/ghostnet.json

# --- runtime ---------------------------------------------------------------
ai/experiments/*
# ...but keep the RESULTS. Weights and plots are large and regenerable; these
# are small JSON records of what a run actually scored and what it was trained
# on. Losing them means a metric nobody can trace back to a dataset or commit.
# Re-enter the run directories, re-exclude everything inside them, then
# whitelist the few small files. Un-ignoring the directory alone lets every
# plot and sample batch back in -- 8.7 MB on the first run.
!ai/experiments/*/
ai/experiments/*/*
!ai/experiments/*/test_metrics.json
!ai/experiments/*/background_metrics.json
!ai/experiments/*/provenance.json
!ai/experiments/*/results.csv
# results.raw.csv is the pre-deduplication original, kept when two resumed
# trainers each wrote a row for the same epoch. It is the evidence that the
# edit to results.csv was a dedup and not a quiet correction of a metric.
!ai/experiments/*/results.raw.csv
# Written notes, and the U-Net scoring record the shipped net model rests on
# (ghostnet/unet.py and promote_net_model.py cite unet-scoring/). Text, a few
# KB each; plots and weights beside them stay ignored.
!ai/experiments/*/*.md
!ai/experiments/unet-scoring/*.json
# notes.md is REQUIRED by EXPERIMENT_GV7_PLAN.md 5 -- "a run with no notes.md
# is not a result" -- and was being dropped by the rule above, which quietly
# made every run unaccountable in the one file that says what it meant.
# The glob covers notes.md and per-metric variants such as notes-centroid.md.
!ai/experiments/*/notes*.md
!ai/experiments/*/centroid_metrics.json
!ai/experiments/*/*_by_size.json

# Review renders are overlays regenerated from queue.csv by
# rank_label_suspects.py --render. 120 of them is 69 MB, and the CSV plus the
# script reproduce them exactly, so the evidence is the queue and not the PNGs.
ai/data/annotate/*/_review/
runs/
*.log
.env
.env.local

# --- os / editor -----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# ...but always keep the directory markers.
!**/.gitkeep

# Demo assets. The sonar input and the reference reports ship, so a clone can
# reproduce the exact run the docs describe (see demo/RAW_DATA.md). Everything
# else in here is per-machine or per-run and goes stale: the survey id, the
# table dumps, the extracted frames keyed by detection ref.
demo/*
!demo/RAW_DATA.md
!demo/NBP0505_line01B_demo.xtf
!demo/reports/
demo/reports/*
!demo/reports/NBP0505_line01B_full_survey.csv
!demo/reports/NBP0505_line01B_full_survey.json

# The showcase fixture DOES ship. It is 14 small frames plus a manifest, and
# without them scripts/showcase_seed.py cannot run on a fresh clone -- the
# frames are drawn from ai/data/processed/, which is rebuilt rather than
# committed, so "re-stage it yourself" would mean downloading eight datasets
# first. The manifest records the original filename and source dataset of every
# frame, which is the provenance the plan's licensing section asks for.
!demo/showcase/
!demo/showcase/manifest.json
!demo/showcase/frames/
!demo/showcase/frames/**

# The per-class .xtf containers themselves stay out -- `*.xtf` above already
# ignores them and they are 6.4 MB each. They are generated from the showcase
# frames, which DO ship, so `scripts/build_demo_xtf.py` rebuilds them on a
# clone in about half a minute. The README explaining that does ship.
!demo/xtf/
!demo/xtf/README.md

# Local rollback snapshots: a 19 MB copy of weights git already tracks.
# Safety net for a bad promotion, not history.
ai/models/_rollback/

# Despeckled dataset copy, built by ai/scripts/build_despeckled.py.
# Derived from processed/, ~4 GB, rebuildable in minutes.
ai/data/processed_despeckled/

# --- derived segmentation dataset ------------------------------------------
# ai/data/net_seg/ is BUILT, not authored: build_net_seg_dataset.py copies the
# 73 chips out of ai/data/processed/ and converts the labelme polygons in
# ai/data/annotate/ghost_net_seg/labels/ into YOLO-seg txt. Both inputs are in
# git, so the 24 MB of images and their derived labels are reproducible and
# stay out. The two small records that say WHICH build this was -- the split
# counts and the dataset_version hash the runs assert against -- are kept, for
# the same reason ai/experiments/ keeps provenance.json.
ai/data/net_seg/*
!ai/data/net_seg/data.yaml
!ai/data/net_seg/build_report.json

# --- visual reference plates -----------------------------------------------
# The underwater and sea-surface photographs the water/sky labs were built to
# reproduce are WATERMARKED ADOBE STOCK COMPS (516851283, 236122432, 76278833).
# They are unlicensed source material, not our work and not a deliverable, and
# this repository has just finished saying it does not redistribute third-party
# imagery it cannot account for -- see docs/DATA.md. They stay on local disk.
# What ships is the reproduction: docs/WATER_LAB.md and the shader it describes.
docs/WhatsApp*
